IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mda-types`

-- Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, Part 3: the evidence rules (ss 15, 16), the presumptions (ss 17 to 22), the protection of informers (s 23), and the
-- certificates of previous admissions and convictions (ss 33(4AC) to (4AE), 33A(3) and (4)).
-- Source: source/MDA1973.txt lines 1439 to 1699 (ss 15 to 23), 2590 to 2620 (s 33(4AC) to (4AE)), 2870 to 2884 (s 33A(3), (4)).
--
-- The question this module answers: WHAT DOES THE COURT PRESUME, AND WHAT MAY IT ADMIT?  Each presumption is a rule over what is PROVED and what
-- the accused proves to the contrary ("until the contrary is proved"; for s 17, "unless it is proved that ... was not for that purpose").  The accused's
-- rebuttal is a fact; the Act does not say to what standard, so the encoding does not either (the Evidence Act 1893 s 3 defines "proved"; see
-- sg/evidence-act-1893 and NOTES.md section 4).  A presumption's outcome is what the offence rules in mda-offences.l4 take as their `... is presumed`
-- input.

§ `17. Presumption concerning trafficking`

-- 17: a person PROVED to have had in his possession MORE THAN (a) 100 grammes of opium, (b) 3 of morphine, (c) 2 of diamorphine, (d) 15 of cannabis, (e)
-- 30 of cannabis mixture, (f) 10 of cannabis resin, (g) 3 of cocaine, (h) 25 of methamphetamine, (ha) 113 of ketamine, or (i) 10 of any or any
-- combination of MDMA, MDA and MDEA, "whether or not contained in any substance, extract, preparation or mixture", is presumed to have had that drug
-- in possession for the purpose of trafficking "unless it is proved that his or her possession of that drug was not for that purpose".  The thresholds are
-- "more than": the quantity equal to the figure does not engage the presumption.  The morphine figure counts morphine in opium and in any other drug.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 17(a) to (i)"
GIVEN q IS A `Drug Quantity Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quantity possessed exceeds a figure in section 17` IF
        q's `the weight of opium in grammes` GREATER THAN 100
    OR  (q's `the weight of morphine in the opium in grammes` PLUS q's `the weight of morphine in the controlled drug, opium excluded, in grammes`) GREATER THAN 3
    OR  q's `the weight of diamorphine in grammes` GREATER THAN 2
    OR  q's `the weight of cannabis in grammes` GREATER THAN 15
    OR  q's `the weight of cannabis mixture in grammes` GREATER THAN 30
    OR  q's `the weight of cannabis resin in grammes` GREATER THAN 10
    OR  q's `the weight of cocaine in grammes` GREATER THAN 3
    OR  q's `the weight of methamphetamine in grammes` GREATER THAN 25
    OR  q's `the weight of ketamine in grammes` GREATER THAN 113
    OR  q's `the weight of N,alpha-dimethyl-3,4-(methylenedioxy)phenethylamine, alpha-methyl-3,4-(methylenedioxy)phenethylamine and N-ethyl-alpha-methyl-3,4-(methylenedioxy)phenethylamine together in grammes` GREATER THAN 10

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 17"
GIVEN q IS A `Drug Quantity Facts`, p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession for the purpose of trafficking is presumed under section 17` IF
        p's `the accused is proved to have had the thing in his or her possession`
    AND `the quantity possessed exceeds a figure in section 17` q
    AND NOT p's `the accused proves that his or her possession of the thing was not for the purpose of trafficking`

§ `18. Presumption of possession and knowledge of controlled drugs`

-- 18(1): a person proved to have had in his possession or custody or under his control (a) anything containing a controlled drug, (b) the keys of
-- anything containing one, (c) the keys of any place or premises or part in which one is found, or (d) a document of title or other document intended
-- for the delivery of one, "is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have had that drug in his or her possession".  18(2): a person proved or presumed
-- to have had a controlled drug in possession "is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have known the nature of that drug".  18(3): the presumptions
-- "are not to be rebutted by proof that the accused never had physical possession".  18(4): where one of 2 or more persons with the knowledge and consent
-- of the rest has a controlled drug in possession, it is deemed to be in the possession of each and all.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 18(1) and (3)"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession of the drug is presumed under section 18(1)` IF
        (   p's `the accused is proved to have had in his or her possession or custody or under his or her control anything containing the thing`
         OR p's `the accused is proved to have had in his or her possession or custody or under his or her control the keys of anything containing the thing`
         OR p's `the accused is proved to have had in his or her possession or custody or under his or her control the keys of a place or premises or part of them in which the thing is found`
         OR p's `the accused is proved to have had in his or her possession or custody or under his or her control a document of title relating to the thing or another document intended for its delivery`)
    AND NOT p's `the accused proves that he or she did not have the thing in his or her possession`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 18(2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knowledge of the nature of the drug is presumed under section 18(2)` IF
        (   p's `the accused is proved to have had the thing in his or her possession`
         OR `possession of the drug is presumed under section 18(1)` p)
    AND NOT p's `the accused proves that he or she did not know the nature of the thing`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 18(4)"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the drug is deemed to be in the possession of each and all of the persons` IF
    p's `one of 2 or more persons with the knowledge and consent of the rest has the thing in his or her possession`

§ `18A. Presumption of possession and knowledge of psychoactive substances`

-- 18A(1) and (3), (4) are the same as 18(1), (3), (4) for a psychoactive substance.  18A(2): a person proved or presumed to have had a psychoactive
-- substance in possession is presumed, until the contrary is proved, (a) to have known that it has the capacity to have a psychoactive effect, and (b) to
-- not believe, and to have had no reason to believe, that it is an excluded substance.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 18A(1) and (3)"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession of the psychoactive substance is presumed under section 18A(1)` IF
    `possession of the drug is presumed under section 18(1)` p

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 18A(2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knowledge of the psychoactive substance is presumed under section 18A(2)` IF
    `knowledge of the nature of the drug is presumed under section 18(2)` p

§ `19, 20, 21, 22. Premises, ship or aircraft, vehicle, urine test`

-- 19(1): where a pipe, syringe, utensil, apparatus or other article intended for smoking, administration or consumption of a controlled drug or
-- psychoactive substance is found in a place or premises, it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the place is used for that purpose.  19(2): a
-- person found in or escaping from a place or premises PROVED OR PRESUMED to be so used is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have been
-- smoking, administering or consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance there.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 19(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Place Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place is presumed to be used for consumption under section 19(1)` IF
        p's `a pipe, syringe, utensil, apparatus or other article intended for smoking, administration or consumption of a controlled drug or psychoactive substance is found in the place or premises`
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 19(2)"
GIVEN p IS A `Place Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to have been consuming in the place under section 19(2)` IF
        p's `the accused was found in, or escaping from, the place or premises`
    AND (   p's `the place or premises is proved to be used for smoking, administering or consuming a controlled drug or psychoactive substance`
         OR `the place is presumed to be used for consumption under section 19(1)` p)
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

-- 20: if a controlled drug or psychoactive substance is found in any ship or aircraft, "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the drug or
-- psychoactive substance has been imported in that ship or aircraft with the knowledge of the master or the captain thereof".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 20"
GIVEN p IS A `Place Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `import with the knowledge of the master or captain is presumed under section 20` IF
        p's `the thing was found in a ship or aircraft`
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

-- 21: if found in any vehicle, it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, "to be in the possession of the owner of the vehicle and of the person in
-- charge of the vehicle for the time being".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 21"
GIVEN p IS A `Place Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession by the accused is presumed under section 21` IF
        p's `the thing was found in a vehicle`
    AND (   p's `the accused is the owner of the vehicle`
         OR p's `the accused is the person in charge of the vehicle for the time being`)
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

-- 22: if a controlled drug or psychoactive substance is found in the urine of a person "as a result of BOTH urine tests conducted under section
-- 31(4)(b)", he or she is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have consumed it in contravention of section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 22"
GIVEN p IS A `Place Presumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consumption is presumed under section 22` IF
        p's `the thing was found in the urine of the accused as a result of both urine tests conducted under section 31(4)(b)`
    AND NOT p's `the contrary is proved`

§ `15 and 16. Certificates`

-- 15: a document purporting to be issued by or on behalf of the government of a country outside Singapore and to state the terms of a corresponding law
-- is admitted in evidence in any proceedings for an offence under the Act on its production by the prosecution without further proof, and is conclusive
-- evidence that (a) it is so issued, (b) the terms of the law are as stated, and (c) any fact stated in it as constituting an offence under that law
-- does constitute one.  "Conclusive": no fact about the contrary is read.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 15(1) and (2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document of a corresponding law is admitted without further proof` IF
        e's `the document purports to be issued by or on behalf of the government of a country outside Singapore and to state the terms of a corresponding law in force there`
    AND e's `the prosecution produces the document or certificate`

-- 16(1): a certificate purporting to be signed by an analyst employed by the Health Sciences Authority or the Home Team Science and Technology Agency, or
-- by a person the Minister appoints (the appointment must be published in the Gazette, 16(2)), and to relate to a controlled drug, controlled substance or
-- psychoactive substance, is admitted in evidence on its production by the prosecution without proof of signature and, "until the contrary is proved, is
-- proof of all matters contained therein".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 16(1)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the analyst's certificate is admitted without proof of signature` IF
        e's `the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst employed by the Health Sciences Authority or the Home Team Science and Technology Agency, or by a person the Minister has appointed by notification in the Gazette`
    AND e's `the certificate purports to relate to a controlled drug, controlled substance or psychoactive substance`
    AND e's `the prosecution produces the document or certificate`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 16(1)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the analyst's certificate is proof of all matters contained in it` IF
        `the analyst's certificate is admitted without proof of signature` e
    AND NOT e's `the contrary is proved`

-- 33(4AC): a certificate purporting to be signed by an officer authorised by the Commissioner of Prisons and to relate to a person's previous admission
-- to an approved institution is admissible on its production by the prosecution without proof of signature in any proceedings under section 33.  33(4AD):
-- the same for a certificate of the registrar for the subordinate military courts or the Military Court of Appeal relating to a previous conviction under
-- section 34 of the Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972.  33(4AE): "until the contrary is proved, evidence of the matters contained in it".  33A(3) and (4) say
-- the same for proceedings under section 33A.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 33(4AC), 33(4AD), 33A(3) and (4)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate of a previous admission or military conviction is admissible without proof of signature` IF
        (   e's `the certificate purports to be signed by an officer authorised in writing by the Commissioner of Prisons and to relate to a person's previous admission to an approved institution`
         OR e's `the certificate purports to be signed by the registrar for the subordinate military courts or for the Military Court of Appeal and to relate to a person's previous conviction by such a court`)
    AND e's `the prosecution produces the document or certificate`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 33(4AE), 33A(3) and (4)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate of a previous admission or military conviction is evidence of the matters in it` IF
        `the certificate of a previous admission or military conviction is admissible without proof of signature` e
    AND NOT e's `the contrary is proved`

-- 31(6) and 31A(4): a certificate stating the result of a urine test (or hair test) must be signed by an analyst employed by the Health Sciences
-- Authority or any other person the Minister appoints (by notification in the Gazette); 31(7) and 31A(5): it may be signed by one who did not personally
-- conduct the test as long as it was conducted by another acting under his or her direction.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 31(6), 31(7), 31A(4), 31A(5)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Evidence Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate of a urine test or hair test is validly signed` IF
    e's `the certificate states the result of a urine test or hair test and is signed by an analyst employed by the Health Sciences Authority or a person the Minister has appointed by notification in the Gazette`

§ `23. Protection of informers`

-- 23(1): "Except as provided in subsection (3)", (a) no information for an offence under the Act is to be admitted in evidence in any civil or criminal
-- proceedings, and (b) no witness is obliged to disclose the name and address of any informer or to answer a question the answer to which would lead, or
-- would tend to lead, to the discovery of the informer.  23(3): the court may permit inquiry and require full disclosure if (a) in proceedings before a
-- court for an offence under the Act, the court, after full inquiry, is satisfied that an informer wilfully made a material statement which he knew or
-- believed to be false or did not believe to be true, or (b) in any other proceedings, the court is of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done
-- between the parties without the disclosure.  Compare section 36 of the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, which says "obliged OR PERMITTED" and
-- "complaints"; section 23 says "obliged" and "information", and has no "or permitted".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 23(3)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Informer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may permit inquiry and require full disclosure concerning the informer` IF
        (   i's `the proceedings are before a court for an offence under this Act`
        AND i's `the court, after full inquiry into the case, is satisfied that an informer wilfully made a material statement which he or she knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true`)
    OR  (   NOT i's `the proceedings are before a court for an offence under this Act`
        AND i's `in proceedings other than for an offence under this Act, the court is of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done between the parties without the disclosure of the name of an informer`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 23(1)(a)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Informer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `information for an offence under the Act is excluded from evidence by section 23(1)(a)` IF
        i's `the proceedings are civil or criminal proceedings`
    AND NOT `the court may permit inquiry and require full disclosure concerning the informer` i

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 23(1)(b)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Informer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a witness may be required to disclose the name and address of the informer` IF
    `the court may permit inquiry and require full disclosure concerning the informer` i
